# InstantDB Data Hooks

- Access Instant through a single schema-typed client (`src/lib/instant/db.ts`). Always pass `schema` to `init`.
- Encapsulate every Instant query or write in a dedicated custom hook; components must not call `db.useQuery` / `db.transact` directly.
- Reads use `db.useQuery` inside the existing per-feature hooks. Keep hook names and `{ data, isPending }` return shapes stable.
- Client writes use `db.transact` (optimistic with automatic rollback). Privileged writes (role assignment, join-code redeem, billing, account deletion, upload finalize) go through the Bun admin server (`adminPost` / `adminGet`).
- Mutations that hit the admin server use `useAsyncAction`. Close Credenza/Dialog immediately on submit; reopen only on failure.
- Index every field used in Instant `where` / `order` (queries error otherwise).
- Preserve strict TypeScript types; use `InstaQLEntity<AppSchema, "entity">` or `Id<"entity">` from `@/lib/ids`. Do not use `any`.
- Do not introduce TanStack Query for Instant data. Admin GET helpers may use a small local-state hook (`useAdminQuery`).

## Reference examples

- Instant client: `src/lib/instant/db.ts`
- Admin fetch: `src/lib/api/admin.ts`
- Async mutation: `src/hooks/useAsyncAction.ts`
